      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T13:23:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, what should we do if they don\u0027t correspond?\nThe assert calls below will panic, but we might also just return  a failure.\n\nI think the 2 options that make sense are:\n- Unconditionally panic if it\u0027s wrong, ideally with a helpful error message. I\u0027d do that by making this function return bool and then having one assert on it.\n- Don\u0027t bother checking at all.",
      "parentUuid": "fc5bea95_73b28fa8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 233,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 233,
        "endChar": 22
